# netsurf: padding is never negative (patch 338)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 337)
#
# A calc() padding that came out negative was used as-is (CSS clamps it to
# 0 at computed-value time). MDN pads its page grid with max(1rem,
# calc(50vw - 720px + 1rem)). Once 339 made that sum exact, its inner
# calc() was -224px.
#
#  - layout_internal.h: both padding resolutions (the box dimensions and
#    the min/max-width outer sum) clamp a negative length to 0.
#
# Gate: CSS-calc-negative legs 2-3 (CALCNEG339).
